; A purchase written cash first records its implied price on the cash
; side ($ 0.01 AAPL), so AAPL is the commodity $ is priced in and
; bal --market values $ in AAPL, exactly as it does without --download.
; prefetch_quotes() follows that recorded direction: it requests $ in
; terms of AAPL in the batch call, the same request the report itself
; makes per commodity, and never AAPL in terms of $.  (A stock written
; first, with "@", or with a P directive is priced in $; see
; prefetch-quotes-posting-priced.test.)

2024/01/15 Buy
    Assets:Checking        $-1000.00
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL

test bal --market --now 2030/06/15 --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote-batch-only.sh
          5.000 AAPL  Assets
         10.000 AAPL    Brokerage
         -5.000 AAPL    Checking
--------------------
          5.000 AAPL
end test

test pricedb --now 2030/06/15 --download --getquote $sourcepath/test/scripts/mock-getquote-batch-only.sh
P 2024/01/15 00:00:00 $ 0.010 AAPL
P 2024/06/15 00:00:00 $ 0.005 AAPL
end test
